  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 312 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nA chilly start to Saturday is expected, as lows hover around the \nfreezing mark, with potential for frost across most of the region. \nSoutherly winds across the region will keep things feeling on the \ncold side, with wind chills in the upper teens to lower 20s across \nthe region. However, by the afternoon, upper level ridging begins to \ntrack across the region, which should usher in some more seasonal \nhigh temperatures through the weekend. Typical highs for the weekend \nare around 63 to 65 degrees. The latest forecast brings highs around \nthe mid 60s to lower 70s, so right around to slightly warmer than \ntypical. This will also usher in slightly warmer overnight lows, as \nwell, with lows Sunday and Monday morning expected to be in the \nupper 30s to lower 40s. \n\nAs the northern jet remains north of the region early next week, \nexpect that our temperatures will return to slightly above seasonal \naverage, with highs returning to the low to mid 70s. Also expect to \nsee lows climbing back into the 40s, potentially the lower 50s in \nspots. This should also keep a fairly dry and quiet weather pattern \nthrough at least mid week. However, long range guidance does suggest \nthe potential for another upper level trough to arrive sometime \naround mid week, which may bring additional rain chances mid to late \nweek.",
